<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SUB-PAGE EXIT. The exact reverse of subpage_enter.xml, and nothing more.

  translationX 0 -> @dimen/space_16 and alpha 1 -> 0, together, over
  @integer/motion_subpage_exit 195ms on @interpolator/ease_standard
  (32-master-plan-android.md 7.3, row "Sub-page exit").

  Two rules are doing the work here and both are easy to get wrong:

  1. Exit is 75% of enter (00-rules.md 3.7, 8.5). 195 is 75% of the 260 in
     subpage_enter.xml — §7's «простое проявление 260 мс» — and it is held as
     @integer/motion_subpage_exit so the pair cannot drift when the reveal tempo is
     retuned. It is NOT the desktop's old flat 150 and it is NOT the same 260
     played backwards.
  2. The curve changes with the direction. Enter settles, so it is ease_out_quint;
     leaving is a two-way state change the eye is not following, so it is
     ease_standard. Reusing quint on the way out makes the page hang at the end
     of its travel.

  The page leaves toward +16dp, i.e. back the way it came in, so open and close
  read as one gesture reversed. Copy is Russian and the app is LTR only; there is
  no RTL mirror here because the platform does not mirror window animations and
  the product ships no RTL locale.

  Transform and alpha only (00-rules.md 8.7). Reduced motion: apply through
  ui/component/SubPage.kt, never by hand - see the note in subpage_enter.xml.
-->
<set xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:duration="@integer/motion_subpage_exit"
    android:fillAfter="false"
    android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_standard"
    android:shareInterpolator="true">

    <translate
        android:fromXDelta="0"
        android:toXDelta="@dimen/space_16" />

    <alpha
        android:fromAlpha="1.0"
        android:toAlpha="0.0" />

</set>
